# Content-builder source integrity

- Never invent **expectation wording**. Quote `lms/seeds/` or the Ministry PDF extract. Cite file path and code.
- Never invent **resource URLs**, **answer keys**, or **licences**. If unknown, set the field to null / `unknown` and say so.
- Preserve `id`, `source`, `source_id`, `source_url`, `source_revision` on every record.
- Pin revisions. Refresh sources deliberately (`git fetch` in `cache/`), inspect, re-index affected records.
- Keep downloaded collections in `content-builder/cache/` (ignored). Commit selected records, provenance, and permitted assets only.
- MathNet is olympiad-oriented. Use it selectively. Keep original provenance beside the dataset licence.
- GeoGebra: record non-commercial usage conditions. Desmos: public embed code only — no calculator API key.
